CloudBurrow patch 3 of 6 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1061; the gap: #976, #986).

The gap: DROP TABLE FUNCTION was refused by the analyzer, "Statement not
supported: DropTableFunctionStatement", because v0.3.1 does not list
ResolvedDropTableFunctionStmt among the statements it accepts, so a table
function could not be dropped or replaced. The patch accepts it and carries
it out as DROP FUNCTION is carried out for a function: the table function is
taken out of the catalog (Catalog.DeleteTVFSpec, which v0.3.1 already has
for TEMP table functions) and its stored spec deleted; IF EXISTS of one that
is not there does nothing. drop_table_function_test.go fails without the
patch and passes with it.

